# FullWorth needs no .env file. This one exists to show you what CAN be changed, not what must be.
#
#   docker compose up -d
#
# There used to be a FULLWORTH_SECRET here, and it was the worst idea in this project: one string
# that was at the same time the database password, the internal key that lets its holder act as any
# user, the ingest key, the banking key and the Codex bridge key. Anything that learned it owned the
# installation. Every secret is now created separately, by the process that reads it, and never
# leaves the server.
#
# FULLWORTH_DOMAIN is gone too. The installation learns the address you reach it at from your first
# registration, and derives the passkey relying party, the passkey origin, the Enable Banking
# redirect and the host pin from it.

# --- Optional ---

# Pin a version instead of following :latest.
# FULLWORTH_VERSION=1.3.0-alpha.35

# Where the container publishes. Keep the bind on 127.0.0.1 and put a reverse proxy with HTTPS in
# front of it: passkeys need a real certificate, and so does anything holding your bank data.
# FULLWORTH_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
# FULLWORTH_PORT=8080

# --- Settings that now live in the app, not here ---
#
#   Sign-in providers (Google, Apple)   admin menu → Anmeldeanbieter
#   FinTS product id                    Einstellungen
#   Enable Banking application + key    Einstellungen → Bankverbindung
#   AI access                           Einstellungen → KI-Zugang
#   Cloud Intelligence                  Intelligence → FullWorth Cloud
#
# Each of them still accepts an environment variable if you would rather set it here — a value you
# state explicitly always wins over a stored one. None of them requires it.
